[?2004l[?2004hroot@595343f7d16a:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> An investigation into potential software vulnerabilities (CVEs) as entry vectors was conducted. Based on system logs, scanner results, and threat intelligence, **no software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited** to gain entry to `redis-prod-01`. The initial access was purely driven by application misconfiguration.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Assessment & Findings
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Automated Vulnerability Scan Results
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Scanner Feed**: The security scanner output file `/sas/vulns.json:1` returned an empty list `[]` (`/sas/vulns.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: No unpatched CVEs were flagged or detected on the target host by vulnerability scanning components.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Reconciliation of Stale Ticket Claims (BlueKeep False Lead)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Draft Change Ticket Claim**: Row 2 of `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10` proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)` on `RDP` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Forensic Assessment**: **INVALID / INCORRECT**.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability in Microsoft Windows Remote Desktop Services (RDP).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - The target system `redis-prod-01` is running Linux Debian 12 (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), and no RDP services are installed or exposed (`/disk/etc/passwd:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Threat Intelligence confirms the entry vector was unauthenticated Redis access (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Actual Entry Vector: Application Misconfiguration
[?2004l[?2004h> - Rather than a software vulnerability exploit, initial access was facilitated by severe administrative misconfiguration of the Redis service:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - **Protected Mode Disabled**: `protected-mode no` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - **Unrestricted Binding**: `bind 0.0.0.0` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - **No Authentication**: `no password set` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - This configuration allowed remote unauthenticated clients to connect directly and issue administrative Redis commands, including `CONFIG SET` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Conclusion & Confidence Statement
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Confidence Level**: **HIGH**.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Entry Vector Classification**: Misconfiguration / Weak Authentication (ATT&CK T1133) rather than Vulnerability Exploitation (ATT&CK T1190).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@595343f7d16a:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline Configuration Assessment Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> A security baseline evaluation was performed against host `redis-prod-01` by inspecting `/sas/baseline.json:1` and system configuration files under `/disk/etc/`. Critical baseline controls failed, directly enabling unauthenticated remote code execution and persistent compromise.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Audit & Findings
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Check CHK-05: Redis Configuration Baseline (`BAS-01`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Target File**: `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/sas/baseline.json:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:18`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Status**: **FAILED / CRITICAL**.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3` contains:
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```text
[?2004l[?2004h>   Redis protected-mode no; bind 0.0.0.0; no password set
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiencies Identified**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   1. **Unrestricted Network Binding (`bind 0.0.0.0`)**: Listens on all IPv4 interfaces rather than loopback (`127.0.0.1`) or a dedicated private internal management network.
[?2004l[?2004h>   2. **Protected Mode Disabled (`protected-mode no`)**: Disables built-in protection that restricts queries from non-loopback interfaces when no password is set.
[?2004l[?2004h>   3. **Missing Authentication (`no password set`)**: Omits `requirepass` authentication directive, granting full administrative control to any network client. M[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[C[K.
[?2004l[?2004h>   4. **Dangerous Command Availability**: High-risk Redis commands (`CONFIG`, `SAVE`, `MODULE`, `EVAL`) were not renamed or disabled.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Secondary System Baseline Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Dynamic Linker Preload Controls (`/etc/ld.so.preload`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Status**: **FAILED**.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1` contains an unmonitored pre-load entry pointing to `/lib/.hide.so` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiency**: Absence of file integrity monitoring (FIM) or write restriction on `/etc/ld.so.preload` enabled silent dynamic linker hijacking.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Temp Directory Execution Permissions (`/tmp`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Status**: **FAILED**.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Executable binaries were staged and executed directly from `/tmp/.redis/` (`/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi`, `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiency**: Mount options for `/tmp` omitted `noexec`, allowing untrusted binaries to run.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> --- 
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Required Baseline Hardening Baseline Specifications
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Enforce `bind 127.0.0.1` or internal IP in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Enforce `protected-mode yes` in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Set strong authentication via `requirepass <complex_password>` in `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (`/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. Rename or disable dangerous Redis commands (`rename-command CONFIG ""`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. Implement FIM alerts on `/etc/ld.so.preload` (`/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`) and crontabs (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@595343f7d16a:/app# ls -l /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md
[?2004l-r--r--r-- 1 root root 1199 Aug 16 14:28 /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md
